name mapnet-lus-synsets
# README: "mapping_lus_synsets.txt" holds a frame, a lexical unit and a WordNet 1.6 synset on each row. The frame is
# as FrameNet names it, the lexical unit as written (bejewelled.a); the synset is a WordNet 1.6 offset, a key of an
# edition no other source here has.
match mapping_lus_synsets.txt

tier row by \n
names frames lus synsets
tier field by \t

thing row frames lus
type frames fnframe node
content lus synsets
# README: "file 'mapping_lus_synsets.txt': mapping between FrameNet frames, lus and WordNet synsets" ... "All frames and
# lexical units included in the resource are described in FrameNet v. 1.3": the lexical unit is a value of FrameNet's
# lexical units, [Buildings, hall.n] (Laplace-Engine#32). Compose that same two-part identity instead of treating
# hall.n as an unqualified lexical unit. A WordNet 1.6 offset remains that edition's own identifier, never a guessed
# equivalence to a different edition's synset. The row states its correspondence to that identifier.
value fnframe frames
attest row frames
pair row synsets
